# apps/cms (jest 26.x/CRA-era @types) and apps/public (jest 30.x/current
# @types) need incompatible major versions of several same-named packages
# (jest + @jest/*, babel-*-jest, expect, pretty-format, @types/react(-dom),
# @types/jest). pnpm's default shared hoist folder can only hold one version
# per name and picks arbitrarily, breaking whichever app didn't win. These
# exclusions force each app to resolve them from its own declared deps.
#
# jest-watch-typeahead is allowed back in below: it's a real react-scripts
# dependency, unrelated to the collision above — excluding it broke
# apps/cms's `test` script.
#
# Do NOT remove the @types/react / @types/react-dom exclusions to "fix"
# apps/cms's build — verified that trades it for a different regression in
# apps/public's build (duplicate @types/react module identity). apps/cms's
# actual build fix lives in root package.json's `pnpm.packageExtensions`
# (declares @types/react as a peerDependency for react-dropzone and other
# packages that bundle untyped .d.ts files) — not here.
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!jest
hoist-pattern[]=!jest-*
hoist-pattern[]=jest-watch-typeahead
hoist-pattern[]=!@jest/*
hoist-pattern[]=!babel-jest
hoist-pattern[]=!babel-preset-jest
hoist-pattern[]=!babel-plugin-jest-hoist
hoist-pattern[]=!expect
hoist-pattern[]=!pretty-format
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/jest
